# Copy to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env (already gitignored).

# SQLite by default for zero-setup local dev. Swap to a hosted Postgres
# connection string (Supabase, Neon) before production, same as LaneMatch.
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# NextAuth
NEXTAUTH_SECRET="generate-with: openssl rand -base64 32"
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# Anthropic API key for the "structure my upload with AI" assistant on the
# grower/processor/broker listing form (lib/ai-listing.ts). Without it, that
# button shows a "not configured" message and sellers just fill the form by
# hand — see console.anthropic.com for a key.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""

# Vercel Blob Storage — where uploaded listing photos/videos, invoices, and
# proof-of-delivery documents actually live (lib/media.ts). Auto-provisioned
# by `vercel blob create-store` and synced to every Vercel environment; for
# local dev, `vercel env pull` (or copy it from the Vercel dashboard) into
# your own .env.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""

# Resend — powers the self-service "forgot password" email (lib/email.ts),
# a welcome email on public self-signup (lib/email.ts's sendWelcomeEmail,
# fired off the critical path in signup/actions.ts), AND real marketing
# email to leads (lib/lead-email.ts's sendEmailToLead, the "Email"/"Email
# later" buttons and the Email channel on the AI campaign composer).
# Without it, /forgot-password shows an honest "not configured yet, ask an
# Admin/AE to reset it for you" message, the welcome email silently no-ops
# (signup itself is never blocked or delayed by this), and the Email
# channel in the Marketing Suite is disabled with a note — never a silent
# failure to send. Sign up at resend.com for a key;
# RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS defaults to Resend's own sandbox sender if unset
# (fine for testing, not for real users — verify a real sending domain
# before launch). The CAN-SPAM-required physical mailing address in every
# marketing email's footer is hardcoded in lib/lead-email.ts
# (BUSINESS_MAILING_ADDRESS) — update it there if the business address
# ever changes.
RESEND_API_KEY=""
RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS=""

# Google Maps Platform — powers real address geocoding at signup
# (lib/geocoding.ts, server-side only). Without it, addresses stay free
# text exactly as before (an honest no-op, not an error). Needs a Google
# Cloud project with billing enabled and the Geocoding API turned on —
# console.cloud.google.com.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=""

# Same Google Maps Platform project, but the client-exposed key (NEXT_
# PUBLIC_ so it's inlined into the browser bundle) that renders the live
# shipment-tracking map (components/deal/shipment-timeline.tsx) via the
# Static Maps API. Google Maps keys are designed to be exposed client-side
# — restrict this one by HTTP referrer in the Cloud console, not by
# keeping it secret. Needs the Maps Static API turned on. Without it, live
# tracking still works, just shows raw coordinates instead of a map image.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=""

# VoIP.ms REST API — texting leads from the Marketing Suite
# (lib/voipms-sms.ts). Replaces an earlier Vonage integration (CLAUDE.md
# §57/§65) — same B2B-outreach posture, different provider. Without all
# three set, the "Text" button still renders (nothing hides it), but every
# send attempt returns an honest "not configured" error instead of firing.
# VOIPMS_API_USERNAME is the account login email; VOIPMS_API_PASSWORD is
# the account's own password — confirmed by a real getBalance call, NOT
# the long base64 "Bearer token" value some VoIP.ms account exports
# separately label as being for 3CX/PBX SMS gateway use (that value
# returned invalid_credentials against this REST API; see
# lib/voipms-sms.ts's own comment for the full story). VOIPMS_DID is the
# sending number (digits only, e.g. "6164150990").
#
# Confirmed risk, not hypothetical: VoIP.ms's account-wide API IP
# allowlist IS enabled on this account (confirmed via a live getBalance
# call returning ip_not_enabled once the credentials themselves were
# correct). This app runs on Vercel (serverless, no fixed outbound IP by
# default) — every send will fail until either the allowlist is disabled,
# or a static-egress-IP setup is added, in Main Menu -> SOAP and REST API
# in the portal.
#
# Once deployed, configure this deployment's inbound callback URL in the
# DID's own settings (DID Numbers -> Edit -> Message Service (SMS/MMS) ->
# "SMS/MMS URL Callback (GET Request)" field — NOT the separate "SMS/MMS
# Webhook URL (POST ... JSON)" field, whose exact payload shape isn't
# reliably documented):
#   https://<domain>/api/voipms/inbound-sms?from={FROM}&message={MESSAGE}
# VoIP.ms substitutes {FROM}/{MESSAGE} with the real values before calling
# it — that's what lets a lead's "wrong number" or "stop" reply actually
# reach lib/voipms-inbound.ts and suppress future texts to them.
#
# Also worth checking before real bulk sends: the VoIP.ms DID settings
# page notes Application-to-Person (A2P) business-messaging requirements/
# verification (contact messaging@voip.ms) — a compliance step separate
# from this app's own code, not something this integration resolves.
VOIPMS_API_USERNAME=""
VOIPMS_API_PASSWORD=""
VOIPMS_DID=""

# Authorizes Vercel Cron's own calls to /api/cron/send-scheduled-messages
# (lib/lead-messaging.ts's processDueCampaigns — the mechanism that
# actually fires a lead-message campaign scheduled for a future time, or
# finishes a large "send now" one). Vercel automatically attaches
# `Authorization: Bearer <this value>` to its own cron requests once this
# is set on the deployment; generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`. Not
# needed for local dev (cron never fires there) — this route just skips
# the check entirely when the env var is unset.
CRON_SECRET=""
